# Pairs with UniqueOwner. Reproduces production before #4452 was fixed (#4466):
# an adaptive split may open its window while an online resize is in flight. The split
# commits on T and routes k2 to s2, a shard the resize neither forwards nor
# fences, and the flip carries R's pre-split map, so a router that cached
# (T, s2) keeps serving T/s2 while the registry routes k2 to R/s1.
#
# The base has no split-abandon path (its interlock makes one unreachable), so
# in this mutant a flip can strand a split mid-flight. A second edit lets that
# split count as finished, standing for AbandonRetargetedSplitAsync, so the
# mutant cannot deadlock and the invariant is the only thing TLC can report.
MODULE: UniqueOwnerSplitDuringResize
TARGET: UniqueOwner
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: an adaptive split opens during a resize, so a stale router keeps serving the split target after the flip
PERTURBS: SplitBegin

--- FIND
SplitBegin ==
    /\ sp = "idle"
    /\ rs = "migrating" \/ rz \in {"idle", "purged", "undone"}
--- REPLACE
SplitBegin ==
    /\ sp = "idle"
\* MUTATION: no interlock with an in-flight resize.
--- END

--- FIND
    /\ sg \in {"idle", "done"}
    /\ sp \in {"idle", "done"}
--- REPLACE
    /\ sg \in {"idle", "done"}
\* MUTATION: a split the flip stranded counts as finished (AbandonRetargetedSplitAsync).
    /\ sp \in {"idle", "done"} \/ alias # spCopy
--- END
